[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5103570893","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121812#issuecomment-5103570893","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121812","id":5103570893,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABMDJPzQ","user":{"login":"bruvzg","id":7645683,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2NDU2ODM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7645683?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg","html_url":"https://github.com/bruvzg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-28T11:31:16Z","updated_at":"2026-07-28T11:31:16Z","body":"> I do think removing the explicit value means the documentation won't be surfaced when users google for the keywords INF and -9223372036854775808/ negative value, which (going by the half-dozen bug reports) is how this issue is mostly referenced to. But I understand the reason for removing it.\r\n\r\nDocumentation can include `keywords=\"\"` field, which is used for search but not displayed in UI.\r\n\r\n```diff\r\ndiff --git a/modules/gdscript/doc_classes/@GDScript.xml b/modules/gdscript/doc_classes/@GDScript.xml\r\nindex a84c59b4ee..6f78d07d9a 100644\r\n--- a/modules/gdscript/doc_classes/@GDScript.xml\r\n+++ b/modules/gdscript/doc_classes/@GDScript.xml\r\n@@ -285,11 +285,11 @@\r\n                <constant name=\"TAU\" value=\"6.28318530717959\">\r\n                        The circle constant, the circumference of the unit circle in radians. This is equivalent to [code]PI * 2[/code], or 360 degrees in rotations.\r\n                </constant>\r\n-               <constant name=\"INF\" value=\"inf\">\r\n+               <constant name=\"INF\" value=\"inf\" keywords=\"-9223372036854775808,9223372036854775808,-9223372036854775807,9223372036854775807\">\r\n                        Positive floating-point infinity. This is the result of floating-point division when the divisor is [code]0.0[/code]. For negative infinity, use [code]-INF[/code]. Dividing by [code]-0.0[/code] will result in negative infinity if the numerator is positive, so dividing by [code]0.0[/code] is not the same as dividing by [code]-0.0[/code] (despite [code]0.0 == -0.0[/code] returning [code]true[/code]).\r\n                        [b]Warning:[/b] Numeric infinity is only a concept with floating-point numbers, and has no equivalent for integers. Dividing an integer number by [code]0[/code] will not result in [constant INF] and will result in a run-time error instead.\r\n                </constant>\r\n-               <constant name=\"NAN\" value=\"nan\">\r\n+               <constant name=\"NAN\" value=\"nan\" keywords=\"-9223372036854775808,9223372036854775808,-9223372036854775807,9223372036854775807\">\r\n                        \"Not a Number\", an invalid floating-point value. It is returned by some invalid operations, such as dividing floating-point [code]0.0[/code] by [code]0.0[/code].\r\n                        [constant NAN] has special properties, including that [code]!=[/code] always returns [code]true[/code], while other comparison operators always return [code]false[/code]. This is true even when comparing with itself ([code]NAN == NAN[/code] returns [code]false[/code] and [code]NAN != NAN[/code] returns [code]true[/code]). Due to this, you must use [method @GlobalScope.is_nan] to check whether a number is equal to [constant NAN].\r\n                        [b]Warning:[/b] \"Not a Number\" is only a concept with floating-point numbers, and has no equivalent for integers. Dividing an integer [code]0[/code] by [code]0[/code] will not result in [constant NAN] and will result in a run-time error instead.\r\n```\r\n\r\n<img width=\"751\" height=\"405\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-07-28 at 14 30 35\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/0611556d-2855-4475-8c9b-fd7d3201b230\" />","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5103570893/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5103676960","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121812#issuecomment-5103676960","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121812","id":5103676960,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABMDPuIA","user":{"login":"Arecher","id":10502115,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwNTAyMTE1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10502115?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arecher","html_url":"https://github.com/Arecher","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arecher/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arecher/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arecher/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arecher/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arecher/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arecher/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arecher/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arecher/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arecher/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-28T11:42:25Z","updated_at":"2026-07-28T11:42:25Z","body":"Interesting! That would be an improvement for being able to surface the documentation for sure.\r\n\r\nI could add that if desired, although I do not understand the impact of changing:\r\n\r\n```\r\n--- a/modules/gdscript/doc_classes/@GDScript.xml\r\n+++ b/modules/gdscript/doc_classes/@GDScript.xml\r\n```","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5103676960/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5103722111","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121812#issuecomment-5103722111","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121812","id":5103722111,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABMDSefw","user":{"login":"bruvzg","id":7645683,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2NDU2ODM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7645683?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg","html_url":"https://github.com/bruvzg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-28T11:46:34Z","updated_at":"2026-07-28T11:46:34Z","body":"> I could add that if desired, although I do not understand the impact of changing\r\n\r\nThis is just a part of `diff` file format, ignore it if you adding it manually.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5103722111/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5103974338","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121812#issuecomment-5103974338","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121812","id":5103974338,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABMDh3wg","user":{"login":"Arecher","id":10502115,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwNTAyMTE1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10502115?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arecher","html_url":"https://github.com/Arecher","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arecher/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arecher/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arecher/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arecher/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arecher/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arecher/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arecher/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arecher/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arecher/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-28T12:11:34Z","updated_at":"2026-07-28T12:11:34Z","body":"Is there a way to add an invisible note to the keywords, so if this bug gets fixed in the future, it is clear why these seemingly random int values are in the documentation?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5103974338/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5104026929","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121812#issuecomment-5104026929","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121812","id":5104026929,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABMDlFMQ","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-28T12:17:00Z","updated_at":"2026-07-28T12:17:00Z","body":"There's no bug here, this is undefined behavior in the C++ language, conversions from floating point values to integers are defined as \"If the truncated value cannot fit into the destination type, the behavior is undefined (even when the destination type is unsigned, modulo arithmetic does not apply).\", so we'd have to do some arbitrary decision as to what to make it become in those cases","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5104026929/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5104463246","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121812#issuecomment-5104463246","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121812","id":5104463246,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABMD_tjg","user":{"login":"Arecher","id":10502115,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwNTAyMTE1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10502115?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arecher","html_url":"https://github.com/Arecher","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arecher/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arecher/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arecher/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arecher/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arecher/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arecher/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arecher/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arecher/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arecher/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-28T13:00:42Z","updated_at":"2026-07-28T13:03:40Z","body":"Right, from an implementation standpoint I agree there is no bug, but from a user perspective `int(INF)` returning `-9223372036854775808`* is clearly perceived as a bug due to how unexpected and counterintuitive it is. In issues where this got [discussed](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/100551), there seems to be relative consensus that it should be changed, just not *how* it should be changed (disabled completely, always return 0, return lowest/highest int, etc).","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5104463246/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5104504868","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121812#issuecomment-5104504868","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121812","id":5104504868,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABMECQJA","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-28T13:04:43Z","updated_at":"2026-07-28T13:04:43Z","body":"I disagree that casting `INF` to an `int` should have any reasonable result, any result at all would be wrong I'd say, `INF` is *not* the same as \"the maximum value\" so returning `INT64_MAX` would be incorrect\r\n\r\nBut something to discuss on the issue thread","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5104504868/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5104834416","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121812#issuecomment-5104834416","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121812","id":5104834416,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABMEWXcA","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-28T13:34:41Z","updated_at":"2026-07-28T13:34:41Z","body":"Regardless of what casting `±INF` to `int` *should* do, any change to that logic would be compatibility-breaking and is out of the scope of this PR. For the time being, documenting the existing behavior is sufficient","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5104834416/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5104891497","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121812#issuecomment-5104891497","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121812","id":5104891497,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABMEZ2aQ","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-28T13:39:53Z","updated_at":"2026-07-28T13:39:53Z","body":"Could you squash your commits? See our [pull request guidelines](https://contributing.godotengine.org/en/latest/organization/pull_requests/creating_pull_requests.html#the-interactive-rebase) for more information","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5104891497/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5115683406","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121812#issuecomment-5115683406","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121812","id":5115683406,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABMOsiTg","user":{"login":"Arecher","id":10502115,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwNTAyMTE1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10502115?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arecher","html_url":"https://github.com/Arecher","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arecher/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arecher/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arecher/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arecher/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arecher/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arecher/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arecher/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arecher/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arecher/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-29T09:22:02Z","updated_at":"2026-07-29T09:22:40Z","body":"I'm running into trouble on the last step.  \r\n<img width=\"849\" height=\"85\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/4477afbb-809d-4162-b28f-28312efbed6c\" />\r\n\r\nI presume that in the example line 'better-project-manager' is the name of the branch, so I have done the same.\r\n> git push --force origin better-project-manager\r\n\r\nAny clue what I'm doing wrong?\r\n\r\nThe tutorial also had no information on how to access a branch or switch a branch that already exists online. I obviously was not using Git, and the tutorial is only written with the presumption that you create a branch via git, which (I can only presume) isn't common for users that need to use `rebase -i`. So perhaps that section should start with a small snippet to confirm you have gained and opened the correct branch. When it mentions you need to check against the `upstream/master`, a link to where that is set up (earlier in the tutorial) would also be good. I had overlooked it, and presumed it was a built-in reference (aka, get the up-to-date version of the repository the local 'master' was forked from).\r\n\r\nAlso, while I understand this is more of a Github issue than a Godot specific one, if Godot wants to attract more contributors with different backgrounds, hurdles such having to use git should really be as small as possible. Having a tool with some proper UI would already help a lot with making the process of contributing a lot more accessible. I get it is important, but all of this is a little much to expect for a single-line documentation change.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5115683406/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5115814497","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121812#issuecomment-5115814497","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121812","id":5115814497,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABMO0iYQ","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organi