cher/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arecher/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arecher/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-29T09:41:25Z","updated_at":"2026-07-29T09:47:24Z","body":"Calling push --force only leads to this. I presume something with the branch setup isn't as it expects.\r\n\r\n<img width=\"925\" height=\"151\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/7c078043-855c-4714-b6b5-709a98bec724\" />\r\n\r\nI can set the upstream to the remote, but I do not know the consequences of this.\r\n\r\nEDIT, I might have figured it out. Since I was in the remote branch, it didn't work. When I cloned the repository, I could not access the branches with `checkout`. The only way I could retrieve them was by -a to see all the branches, and then switching to them with '-b' I believe. Likely because they were remote branches, rather than ones made locally?\r\n\r\nI seems that after I do that, checkout *is* possible though. After doing that, it seems to work.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5115940283/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5115987849","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121812#issuecomment-5115987849","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121812","id":5115987849,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABMO_HiQ","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-29T09:44:59Z","updated_at":"2026-07-29T09:45:54Z","body":"Seems you've set the branch up incorrectly perhaps, it should be named \"Document-casting-INF/NAN-to-int-is-undefined-behavior\", I suggest checking it out like the instructions in the tutorial describe ","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5115987849/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":{"reason":"resolved"}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5116279793","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121812#issuecomment-5116279793","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121812","id":5116279793,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABMPQ78Q","user":{"login":"Mickeon","id":66727710,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY2NzI3NzEw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/66727710?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon","html_url":"https://github.com/Mickeon","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-29T10:10:11Z","updated_at":"2026-07-29T10:10:11Z","body":"> Having a tool with some proper UI would already help a lot with making the process of contributing a lot more accessible\r\n\r\nUse [GitHub Desktop](https://desktop.github.com/download/). Among all the options in the menu bar there's one to rebase the current branch.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5116279793/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5128058175","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121812#issuecomment-5128058175","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121812","id":5128058175,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABMaf1Pw","user":{"login":"Arecher","id":10502115,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwNTAyMTE1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10502115?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arecher","html_url":"https://github.com/Arecher","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arecher/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arecher/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arecher/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arecher/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arecher/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arecher/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arecher/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arecher/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arecher/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-30T07:44:46Z","updated_at":"2026-07-30T08:41:32Z","body":"Should be done!\r\n\r\n> Use [GitHub Desktop](https://desktop.github.com/download/). Among all the options in the menu bar there's one to rebase the current branch.\r\n\r\nThis worked *infinitely* better. **Genuinely, please never *ever* link any new/web/documentation-contributor to the tutorial on how to use Git, when Github Desktop is available**. The 4 hours I spent fighting Git yesterday literally ensured I would *never* contribute or even attempt to rebase my branches again. Meanwhile, a simple link to Github Desktop's [documentation ](https://docs.github.com/en/desktop/managing-commits/amending-a-commit-in-github-desktop) would achieve the same, but with a lot less hurdles and confusion for a new user.\r\n\r\nThe documentation for [rebasing](https://docs.github.com/en/desktop/working-with-your-remote-repository-on-github-or-github-enterprise/syncing-your-branch-in-github-desktop#rebasing-your-project-branch-onto-another-branch) is a little less clear, since it doesn't explain *what* a rebase does, but if necessary just link to [squashing commits](https://docs.github.com/en/desktop/managing-commits/squashing-commits-in-github-desktop), which seems to lead to the same result (a single commit) while being having a perfectly clear and logical workflow. (*The only oddity with squashing is that it doesn't let you squash while you are comparing against a different branch*)\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5128058175/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":